hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1730","Waki and Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, both saying: Sufyan narrated to us, from Musab ibn Muhammad, from Yala ibn Abi Yahya, from Fatimah daughter of Husayn, from her father, Abdur-Rahman said: Husayn ibn Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The beggar has a right even if he comes on a horse."
"1731","Waki informed us, Thabit ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Shayban who said: I said to al-Husayn ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: What do you retain from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? He said: I went up with him to the charity room and took a date and chewed it in my mouth. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Throw it, for charity is not lawful for us."
"1732","Ibn Numayr and Yala narrated to us, both saying: Hajjaj meaning Ibn Dinar al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn Khalid, from Husayn ibn Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is speaking little about what does not concern him."
"1733","Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ali asserting from Husayn and Ibn Abbas, or from one of them, that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, only stood because of the funeral of a Jew that was carried past him, and he said: Its odor annoyed me."
"1734","Yazid and Abbad ibn Abbad narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Abi Hisham informed us, Abbad said: Ibn Ziyad, from his mother, from Fatimah daughter of al-Husayn, from her father al-Husayn ibn Ali, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: There is no Muslim man or woman afflicted with a calamity who remembers it, even if its time is long, Abbad said: its time is old, and renews for that the returning to Allah, except that Allah renews for him at that time and gives him the like of its reward on the day he was afflicted with it."
"1735","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Hawra, from al-Husayn ibn Ali who said: My grandfather taught me, or he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, words to say in witr, and he mentioned the hadith."
"1736","Abdul-Malik ibn Amr and Abu Said narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Husayn, from his father Ali ibn Husayn, from his father that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The miser is one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send prayers upon me, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Abu Said said: And he did not send prayers upon me much."
"1737","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ali ibn Husayn, from his father, may Allah Most High be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Part of the excellence of a person's Islam is his leaving what does not concern him."
